# The app icon picked in Settings stays in the Dock and the ⌘-Tab switcher once a download has
# run (GitHub #319). Chromium shows download progress on the Dock tile with a view of its own,
# which drew the bundle's icon: from the first download on, ⌘-Tab showed Segments until the
# icon was picked again. Midnight comes in through the argument domain, so the run never
# writes the defaults the installed Cra reads. Setting the icon again (here on the way back
# from the menu bar) keeps Chromium's view on the tile, so its download badge isn't lost.
# promise: #319
home
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "keepInMenuBar": true}
arg -appIcon
arg midnight
cra://debug?dockTile=before
expect-log dock tile before: view=\S+ draws=picked
cra://open?url=${TRICKLE}/trickle.bin
wait 2
cra://debug?downloadState=started
expect-log download state started: running=true
cra://debug?dockTile=downloading
expect-log dock tile downloading: view=\S+ draws=picked
cra://debug?download=cancel
expect-log download control: cancel
wait 1
cra://debug?dockTile=after
expect-log dock tile after: view=\S+ draws=picked
cra://debug?quit=menu
wait 2
expect-log menu bar: quit keeps Cra in the menu bar
cra://action/newWindow
wait 3
expect-log app icon: \S+ set again, back in the Dock
# The window's tab comes back on the file and downloads it again, under Chromium's badge.
cra://debug?dockTile=returned
expect-log dock tile returned: view=DockTileView draws=picked
cra://debug?download=cancel
wait 1
